      "title": "Search Page",
      "description": "Search Page Apply Give Contact/Directory A-Z Index Calendars See All Jobs Applicant Settings About Stockton Academics Admissions, Scholarships & Aid Campus Life Athletics & Recreation Arts & Culture Alumni & Friends About Stockton Academics Admissions, Scholarships & Aid Campus Life Athletics & Recreation Arts & Culture Alumni & Friends Kiosk mode Skip to jobs search results Category Search categories 7 filter options found Category Academic Affairs (1 items) 1 Athletics and Recreation (1 items) 1 School of Arts & Humanities (15 items) 15 School of Business (14 items) 14 School of General Studies (5 items) 5 School of Natural Science & Mathematics (3 items) 3 School of Social & Behavioral Sciences (7 items) 7 Department Search departments 6 filter options found Department Athletics & Campus Recreation (1 items) 1 School of Arts and Humanities (15 items) 15 School of Business (14 items) 14 School of General Studies (5 items) 5 School of Natural Sciences & Mathematics (3 items) 3 School of Social & Behavioral Sciences (7 items) 7 Employment Type Search employment types 5 filter options found Employment Type Adjunct Faculty (41 items) 41 AFT Professional Staff (1 items) 1 Faculty Full-time (1 items) 1 Management (1 items) 1 Temporary (TES) (1 items) 1 City Search cities 4 filter options found City Atlantic City (4 items) 4 Galloway (38 items) 38 Multiple Locations (2 items) 2 Port Republic (1 items) 1 Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Director of Coastal Research Center (13M) Galloway, New Jersey School of Natural Sciences & Mathematics School of Natural Science & Mathematics Management The Director of the Coastal Research Center provides leadership for Stockton University's applied coastal research, overseeing externally funded projects, strategic partnerships, and Center operations. Reporting to the Dean of the School of Natural Sciences and Mathematics, the Director manages personnel, budgets, contracts, and research activities, while ensuring the delivery of high-quality scientific services. The Director also supports the University's academic mission through student engagement, collaboration with faculty, and contributions to teaching and research, while serving as the Center's primary representative to government agencies, clients, and other external partners.  This is a Grant Funded position with an anticipated start date of October 5, 2026. Read more Assistant Professor of Computer Information Systems, Tenure Track, Starting 09-01-2026 Galloway, New Jersey School of Business School of Business Faculty Full-time The AACSB accredited School of Business at Stockton University invites applications for a full-time tenure track Assistant Professor of Computer Information Systems starting September 1, 2026. Read more Professional Services Specialist 3, Geospatial Team Leader & Environmental Specialist (13M) Port Republic, New Jersey School of Natural Sciences & Mathematics School of Natural Science & Mathematics AFT Professional Staff Stockton University is accepting applications for a Professional Services Specialist 3, Geospatial Team Leader & Environmental Specialist (13M).  This is a Grant Funded position that is anticipated to start on Monday, August 24, 2026.\n\nThe exponential growth of cutting-edge research projects combined with the onslaught of new technological capabilities, increased state and public interest in the health of our coastlines, has created the need for a Geospatial Team Leader & Environmental Specialist for the Coastal Research Center (CRC). Read more TES - Men's Lacrosse Assistant Coach - Intercollegiate Sports Galloway, New Jersey Athletics & Campus Recreation Athletics and Recreation Temporary (TES) Under the direction of the Executive Director of Athletics and Campus Recreation, the Assistant Men's Lacrosse Coach is responsible for the following:\n-  Assist in supervising all practice sessions and contests/competitions.\n-  Assist in supervising and traveling with the team on trips. \n-  Assist in maintaining the team's equipment and uniforms.\n-  Assist in the recruitment of student athletes.\n-  Maintain CPR Certification and annually complete the concussion training course.\n-  Drive vehicles to transport students/staff on campus as well as to off campus events. \n-  Adhere to the rules and regulations of the University, Athletic Office, National Collegiate \n   Athletic Association, New Jersey Athletic Conference or affiliated conferences. \n-  Comply with all medical decisions/protocols from Athletic Training Services. \n-  Perform other duties assigned Read more Adjunct Faculty - School of Natural Science & Mathematics Galloway, New Jersey School of Natural Sciences & Mathematics School of Natural Science & Mathematics Adjunct Faculty The School of Natural Sciences and Mathematics at Stockton University is continuously looking to expand the pool of qualified adjunct faculty (part-time).\n\nPlease visit the School of Natural Sciences and Mathematics webpage www.stockton.edu/nams for additional information about our programs and course offerings. Read more Adjunct Faculty - School of Arts & Humanities, American Studies Galloway, New Jersey School of Arts and Humanities School of Arts & Humanities Adjunct Faculty The School of Arts & Humanities is expanding its pool of qualified adjunct (part-time) instructors. Opportunities may exist to teach a flexible schedule that may include teaching assignments during days and evenings. Services are contracted on a semester/term basis. Read more Adjunct Faculty - School of Arts & Humanities, Visual Arts, Graphic Design, Web Design Galloway, New Jersey School of Arts and Humanities School of Arts & Humanities Adjunct Faculty The School of Arts & Humanities is expanding its pool of qualified adjunct (part-time) instructors. Opportunities may exist to teach a flexible schedule that may include teaching assignments during days and evenings. Services are contracted on a semester/term basis. Read more Adjunct Faculty - School of Arts & Humanities, Visual Arts, Illustration Galloway, New Jersey School of Arts and Humanities School of Arts & Humanities Adjunct Faculty The School of Arts & Humanities is expanding its pool of qualified adjunct (part-time) instructors. Opportunities may exist to teach a flexible schedule that may include teaching assignments during days and evenings. Services are contracted on a semester/term basis. Read more Adjunct Faculty - School of Arts & Humanities, Visual Arts, 3D Design and Sculpture 1 Galloway, New Jersey School of Arts and Humanities School of Arts & Humanities Adjunct Faculty The School of Arts & Humanities is expanding its pool of qualified adjunct (part-time) instructors. Opportunities may exist to teach a flexible schedule that may include teaching assignments during days and evenings. Services are contracted on a semester/term basis. Read more Adjunct Faculty - School of Arts & Humanities, Music-Percussion Instruction Galloway, New Jersey School of Arts and Humanities School of Arts & Humanities Adjunct Faculty The School of Arts & Humanities is expanding its pool of qualified adjunct (part-time) instructors. Opportunities may exist to teach a flexible schedule that may include teaching assignments during days and evenings. Services are contracted on a semester/term basis. Read more Adjunct Faculty - School of Business, Public Law Atlantic City , New Jersey School of Business School of Business Adjunct Faculty The Public Law program, located within the School of Business at Stockton University, accepts applications from qualified adjunct (part-time) instructors. Opportunities may exist to teach an undergraduate or graduate course during the day or evening at our campuses in Atlantic City, Galloway or Manahawkin. Services are contracted on a semester/term basis. Available teaching assignments may vary semester to semester.\n\nThis job will be posted continuously to expand Stock