t-time) instructors. Opportunities may exist to teach a flexible schedule that may include teaching assignments during days and evenings. Services are contracted on a semester/term basis.\n\nSeeking applicants to teach undergraduate level courses in the following areas in all levels:\n - A variety of movement and somatic based techniques including but not limited to modern, ballet, improvisation, jazz, african, tap, dance composition, yoga and pilates.\n - Lecture based courses including but are not limited to Dance History, Dance Pedagogy and Wellness, Senior Seminar, Dance Production, Kinesiology.\n - Movement based courses within General Studies curriculum such as Intro to Dance, Modern Principles, Dance and Culture. Read more Displaying 31 - 45 of 45 in total ‹ 1 2 › Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) d8857c5e Last Name (required) deffcd53 Email (required) 145c818c Job Alert 956bcf09 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Locations Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Office of the President Read Stockton Now Media Resources Do Business With Stockton University Alerts Bookstore Library Employment Safety Information Statements & Policies Additional Locations Atlantic City Hammonton Manahawkin Stockton University 101 Vera King Farris Drive Galloway, NJ 08205-9441 (609) 652-1776 Maps, Directions & Parking Accessibility Statement Facebook Twitter YouTube Instagram LinkedIn Flickr Snapchat TikTok Stockton University is an Equal Opportunity Institution © 2022 Stockton University Candidate Details Please choose the location(s)"
